	 ('60faa620-ff03-4f64-bc83-430da14f3383'::uuid,'WKT 103','Work Term I','Co-op position must be engineering or science related. Routine type of positions are acceptable. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2018-2019/courses/work-term/WKT/103/','2018-2019','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('9709cecc-dfa8-484a-a9a8-b8f4dd895c57'::uuid,'WKT 608','GCM Internship','The GCM internship enables GCM students to obtain relevant workplace experience from an approved company in the graphic communications industry. Assessment includes regular student journal entries, the employer''s assessment of the intern''s performance, and a final report. Throughout assessment, students focus on the application of management theories and practices in the workplace. The course coordinator instructor may visit interns during the term. This course is taken in conjunction with a work term assignment.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2018-2019/courses/work-term/WKT/608/','2018-2019','None','GCM 220 and GCM 370 and GCM 375','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('21f9a259-4e8d-4f4d-aae7-6d39063d3322'::uuid,'WKT 88A/B','Co-operative Internship Program','An optional 16 month work term assignment for students in the Industrial and Mechanical Engineering programs. The selected students will have completed all the academic curricular requirements of the Third Year of the program, and achieved a clear standing. Enrolment in this course is conditional on the student obtaining and accepting an internship placement offer from an approved corporate partner. Interns will be visited as required by the course co-ordinator to assess their progress. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis. Grade achieved at the successful completion of the assignment and the submission of an acceptable work term report is PSD.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2018-2019/courses/work-term/WKT/88AB/','2018-2019','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
