	 ('3714c597-9756-4083-b193-99c7b5af354a'::uuid,'WKT 401','Work Term I','Co-op position must be engineering or science related. Routine type of positions are acceptable. All courses from 1st and 2nd Semester must be successfully completed before enrolling in WKT 401. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/401/','2020-2021','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('aff127cc-2e3b-4aff-8208-0de967beb80f'::uuid,'WKT 110','Work Term I','Co-op position must be health and safety related. Routine type of position is acceptable but project work is encouraged. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/110/','2020-2021','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('f7d0328c-f504-4dd3-8522-e989544f47ad'::uuid,'WKT 125','Work Term I','Co-op position must be related to Economics and Management Science and may be entry-level or junior in responsibility and content. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/125/','2020-2021','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('7ba27edc-75eb-4f34-9b88-99300f8dc2d8'::uuid,'WKT 608','GCM Internship','The GCM internship enables GCM students to obtain relevant workplace experience from an approved company in the graphic communications industry. Assessment includes regular student journal entries, the employer''s assessment of the intern''s performance, and a final report. Throughout assessment, students focus on the application of management theories and practices in the workplace. The course coordinator instructor may visit interns during the term. This course is taken in conjunction with a work term assignment.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/608/','2020-2021','None','GCM 220 and GCM 370 and GCM 375','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('af4946be-b146-4758-940b-84d51d1431aa'::uuid,'WKT 90A/B','Co-operative Internship Program','An optional 12-16 month Work Term assignment for students in the Civil Engineering program. The selected students will have completed all the academic curricular requirements of the third year of the program, and achieved a clear standing. Course enrolment is conditional on the student obtaining and accepting an internship placement offer from an approved corporate partner. Interns will be visited as required by the course co-ordinator to assess their progress. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis. Grade achieved at the successful completion of the assignment and the submission of an acceptable Work Term report is PSD.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/90AB/','2020-2021','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('e5d7d830-9eb3-4b65-8ef4-f6eef5c5cd6c'::uuid,'WKT 312','Work Term III','Enrolment requires a clear academic standing of 5th and 6th semester academic requirements and on the student obtaining and accepting a co-op placement offer from an approved corporate partner.  Co-op position must be in the Hospitality and Tourism industry.  A routine type of position is acceptable but supervisor and/or managerial work is encouraged.  This work term should build on the experience of the 2nd work term. This course is graded on a pass/fail basis.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2020-2021/courses/work-term/WKT/312/','2020-2021','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
