	 ('49a09c01-23bb-4fa0-909f-b2dcadcb4e72'::uuid,'FMF 635','Advanced Accessory Design','Expanding on knowledge gained in Millinery, Jewellery or Small goods: Fur and Leather design, this studio course brings together a multi-disciplined approach through guided and self-directed projects. Through lectures, demonstrations and supporting research, students will design and create innovative pieces using traditional and nontraditional methods. Students are expected to have foundational skills from their area of previous study. Studio Format.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2024-2025/courses/fashion---material-and-fabrication/FMF/635/','2024-2025','None','FMF 235 or FMF 335 or FMF 240 or FSN 502','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('50895106-5f56-4382-89fa-26a13347efe0'::uuid,'FMF 620','Special Topics in Textiles and Material Practices','This practice-led course provides students with a unique opportunity to develop and explore hands-on research in the area of Textile Studies. In the Materials and Fabrication concentration, students will engage in their own original research actively working individually or collaboratively on an innovative potentially interdisciplinary project. Content and approach change each time it is offered. Topics include development of original textiles investigating an exhaustive creative process related to discovery, reinterpretation and the reimagining of materials and techniques.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2024-2025/courses/fashion---material-and-fabrication/FMF/620/','2024-2025','None','FMF 130 or FSN 303','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
religious context in which Sikhism emerged in Punjab at the turn of the  
16th century, as well as an exploration of how this tradition evolved in  
South Asia and around the world until today. It will consider Sikh  
worldviews, beliefs, ritual, practices, and institutions, with a special  
emphasis on Sikhism in Canada.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2024-2025/courses/religious-studies/REL/205/','2024-2025','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
	 ('3af98175-b87a-4424-a9ba-51170aacb5eb'::uuid,'REL 220','Introduction to Christianity','This course is a survey of Christianity. Students will be introduced to distinctively Christian beliefs and practices, its history, institutions, and foundational texts, and its cultural and social influences. An important focus will be three major episodes in Christian thought: the Arian Controversy, the Reformation in Western Christianity, and contemporary developments such as Liberation Theology and Feminist Theology.','https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2024-2025/courses/religious-studies/REL/220/','2024-2025','None','None','None','None',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
